From: Junfeng Yang <didiglobalusa@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:44:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: tag_dsa: only send FORWARD tags from bridged
 ports

dsa_xmit_ll() builds a FORWARD tag whenever skb->offload_fwd_mark is
set, using the bridge number of the egress port to pick the virtual
source device. A standalone port has no bridge: dsa_port_bridge_num_get()
returns 0 and the tag names a device that stands for no bridge at all.
The comment further down in the same function already says that a
standalone port always sends FROM_CPU.

The bridge only sets the mark for ports that offload it, but the mark
can also be left over from reception on another port, for example when
the netfilter flowtable routes a frame from a bridged port straight to a
standalone one.

Look up the bridge first and require one before using FORWARD, so that a
standalone port always sends FROM_CPU.

Fixes: d82f8ab0d874 ("net: dsa: tag_dsa: offload the bridge forwarding process")
Signed-off-by: Junfeng Yang <didiglobalusa@gmail.com>
---

--- a/net/dsa/tag_dsa.c
+++ b/net/dsa/tag_dsa.c
@@ -135,7 +135,9 @@ static struct sk_buff *dsa_xmit_ll(struc
 	enum dsa_cmd cmd;
 	u8 *dsa_header;
 
-	if (skb->offload_fwd_mark) {
+	br_dev = dsa_port_bridge_dev_get(dp);
+
+	if (skb->offload_fwd_mark && br_dev) {
 		unsigned int bridge_num = dsa_port_bridge_num_get(dp);
 		struct dsa_switch_tree *dst = dp->ds->dst;
 
@@ -153,8 +155,6 @@ static struct sk_buff *dsa_xmit_ll(struc
 		tag_port = dp->index;
 	}
 
-	br_dev = dsa_port_bridge_dev_get(dp);
-
 	/* If frame is already 802.1Q tagged, we can convert it to a DSA
 	 * tag (avoiding a memmove), but only if the port is standalone
 	 * (in which case we always send FROM_CPU) or if the port's
